  // over --jtag-port cannot catch a running hart on the bitbang DTM -- its
  // dmstatus never reaches `allhalted` (the hart oscillates
  // unavailable/havereset/running). Uses the same in-process DMI halt the hybrid
  // handoff relies on (ResumeDriver::halt over SystemCDmiBus, which drains every
  // access to completion -- unlike the passive, main-loop-clocked DTM). The
  // debugger then attaches to an already-stopped hart and its `continue`
  // (resumereq) starts execution; the hart fetches one or two crt0 instructions
  // before haltreq takes effect, exactly as the resume path does.
